<SECTION image-layout="blank" background-color="#1A1A1A">
  <DIV class="body">
    <H1><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">Three Systemic Barriers Still Constrain Climate Tech Scale</SPAN></H1>
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[50,50]">
      <DIV>
        <P><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">Despite breakthrough economics, climate technology deployment faces systemic constraints that limit scaling velocity. Regulatory uncertainty creates project development risks that increase capital costs <SPAN text-color="#FF6B35">15-25%</SPAN>. Supply chain bottlenecks for critical minerals and specialized components extend project timelines <SPAN text-color="#FF6B35">18-36 months</SPAN>. Talent shortages across engineering, project development, and operations roles limit organizational capacity to execute at the pace capital availability would otherwise enable. These barriers interact and compound, creating deployment friction that persists despite favorable market fundamentals.</SPAN></P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <UL>
          <LI><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF"><B>Regulatory Uncertainty:</B> Permitting delays and policy inconsistencies increase project risk premiums</SPAN></LI>
          <LI><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF"><B>Supply Chain Bottlenecks:</B> Critical mineral dependencies and component shortages extend development timelines</SPAN></LI>
          <LI><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF"><B>Talent Shortages:</B> Specialized skill gaps limit organizational capacity for rapid scaling</SPAN></LI>
        </UL>
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>